quickstart:
Sign up at modal.com and install the CLI, then decorate a Python function with an image and a GPU — Modal builds the container and autoscales it for you. You are billed per second of actual compute, so functions that scale to zero cost nothing between calls.

```python
# pip install modal && modal setup
import modal

app = modal.App("hello-gpu")
image = modal.Image.debian_slim().pip_install("torch")

@app.function(gpu="T4", image=image)
def check():
    import torch
    return torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)

@app.local_entrypoint()
def main():
    print(check.remote())

# run: modal run hello_gpu.py
```
